The portable C in the scenario start-setup: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/start-setup.txt, see
harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what is
expected in its place.
Deviation: 10 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the box of F10 names the program in its title and in its question, by a
name that is two letters shorter: the box is two cells narrower, a cell on
either side, and its shadow ends a cell further left. Where the box is over
what DOS had shown, with no panel on the left, the cell that it no longer
covers on the left shows what DOS wrote there: the banner, as the portable C
has it, and the commands

